{number: 120}
{title: The Love of God}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
The [C] love of God is greater far
Than [F] tongue or pen can [C] ever tell;
It goes beyond the highest star,
And [G7] reaches to the lowest [C] hell.
The guilty pair, bowed down with care,
God [F] gave His Son to [C] win;
His erring child He reconciled,
And [G7] pardoned from his [C] sin.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
O [F] love of God, how rich and pure!
How [C] measureless and [G7] strong!
It [C] shall forevermore endure
The [G7] saints' and angels' [C] song.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
When [C] hoary time shall pass away,
And [F] earthly thrones and [C] kingdoms fall;
When men who here refuse to pray,
On [G7] rocks and hills and mountains [C] call;
God's love, so sure, shall still endure,
All [F] measureless and [C] strong;
Redeeming grace to Adam's race—
The [G7] saints' and angels' [C] song.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Could [C] we with ink the ocean fill,
And [F] were the skies of [C] parchment made;
Were every stalk on earth a quill,
And [G7] every man a scribe by [C] trade;
To write the love of God above
Would [F] drain the ocean [C] dry;
Nor could the scroll contain the whole,
Though [G7] stretched from sky to [C] sky.
{end_of_verse}
